@1928_main
new-page: true
go-to: main if difficulty >= 0; main.main_easy if difficulty < 0

= 1928

It is a bright time for German democracy. After a period of struggle, inflation is finally under control, and the economy is expanding steadily. In foreign policy, we have reached agreements with the <span style="color: #0A3161;">Western</span> powers and the <span style="color: #750e0e;">**Soviet Union**</span> that might make genuine peace a reality. 

Now, as the center-right government of <span style="color: #000000;">**Wilhelm Marx**</span> in power, the task of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span> is to pass a comprehensive National School Law Bill. Despite our legislative succcesses from our time in government, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Bürgerblock**</span> coalition is on the edge of collapsing. With elections coming up, perhaps our achievements in government will be able to counteract the growing influence of <span style="color: #909090;">**special interest parties**</span>. 
